# Innocent Blood while Bot2 controls no creature: Bot2 has nothing to sacrifice and that does not stop the spell, so the
# caster still sacrifices the creature they control (a single creature is no choice, so no question is asked) - the spell
# does as much as it can (CR 101.3, 608.2c). Bot2's noncreature permanents (a land and a Mox) are untouched: what is
# sacrificed is a creature only.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Ornithopter
Innocent Blood
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Swamp
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Innocent Blood.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp
Bot1.Graveyard = Innocent Blood; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Swamp
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
